    "collapsible_content_YBjywd": {
      "type": "collapsible-content",
      "blocks": {
        "collapsible_row_RjUaji": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What is Grounding?",
            "icon": "check_mark",
            "row_content": "<p>Grounding, or Earthing, is the practice of connecting your body directly to the earth’s natural energy field. This can be as simple as walking barefoot outside or using “barefoot substitutes” like our Grounded Spirit products. Our products connect to the ground port of home outlets or use a ground rod kit to bring the earth’s healing energy indoors. Made with conductive materials, they transfer this energy to your body through direct skin contact, helping you stay balanced, connected, and restored.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_3AY6eH": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What’s the Difference Between Grounding and Earthing?",
            "icon": "check_mark",
            "row_content": "<p>Grounding and Earthing both reconnect you to the Earth’s natural energy, and the terms are often used interchangeably. Some people, however, make a subtle distinction: “Earthing” refers specifically to direct skin contact with the Earth, like walking barefoot on grass or sand, while “Grounding” can also refer to the process of connecting electrical devices to the earth for safety.<br/><br/>For most, these terms are interchangeable when talking about the health benefits of connecting to the Earth’s surface. Whether through direct contact or using our trusted “barefoot substitutes,” like Grounded Spirit products, reconnecting is easy, natural, and restorative.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_rXbXPz": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What’s the Technology Behind Grounding Products?",
            "icon": "check_mark",
            "row_content": "<p>Grounded Spirit products use simple yet effective technology. Each product is made with conductive materials, like silver threading, which allows the Earth’s energy to flow through. When connected via a ground cord to the ground port of an outlet or an optional ground rod, this energy is safely transferred to your body. Our products are designed to be safe, durable, and accessible, with options to fit every lifestyle. Explore how you can bring the healing power of grounding into your everyday life with Grounded Spirit.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_JxdLdW": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How Does Grounding Affect Pets?",
            "icon": "check_mark",
            "row_content": "<p>Just like humans, pets benefit from grounding—especially indoor animals like dogs and cats who rarely connect with the Earth’s natural energy. Grounding can help reduce inflammation, improve circulation, and support overall well-being in pets. It may also ease stress and anxiety, providing a sense of calm.<br/><br/>Many pets instinctively gravitate towards grounding products, like grounded bedsheets, sensing the soothing effects even if they can’t express it. Their actions speak volumes about the natural comfort and healing grounding provides, reminding us that all beings thrive when connected to the Earth.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_hRUENB": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Can Grounding Help with Neuropathy?",
            "icon": "check_mark",
            "row_content": "<ol><li><strong>Improved Blood Flow: </strong>Grounding has been shown to enhance circulation, which may help with neuropathy, especially diabetic neuropathy. Better blood flow supports healing and nerve regeneration in the extremities, where neuropathy commonly affects the hands and feet.</li><li><strong>Reduced Inflammation: </strong>Neuropathy is often linked to nerve damage caused by inflammation. Grounding can help neutralize free radicals, which contribute to inflammation, potentially easing the inflammatory response associated with neuropathy.</li><li><strong>Pain Relief: </strong>Some studies suggest grounding can reduce chronic pain. Since neuropathy involves nerve pain, grounding may provide relief by altering nerve electrical activity or reducing inflammation.</li><li><strong>Stress Reduction: </strong>Grounding induces a calming effect, which can be beneficial since stress can worsen neuropathy symptoms. By reducing stress, grounding may help manage these symptoms more effectively.</li><li><strong>Better Sleep:</strong> Grounding is known to improve sleep quality, which is essential for healing and managing pain. Improved rest can indirectly support neuropathy management, enhancing overall well-being.</li></ol>",
            "page": ""
          }
        }
      },
