    "collapsible_content_h7dBnU": {
      "type": "collapsible-content",
      "blocks": {
        "collapsible_row_ziaMhz": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How to Test My Grounded Spirit™ Sheet or Mat",
            "icon": "check_mark",
            "row_content": "<p>To check if your Grounded Spirit™ product is working, you can use a multimeter or voltmeter, available at most hardware stores. This device measures your body voltage. When your grounding sheet or mat is functioning correctly, your body voltage will decrease as soon as you place any part of your body on it, indicating a connection to the Earth’s energy.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_d964Ut": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Do Grounding Products Emit EMFs or Magnetic Fields?",
            "icon": "check_mark",
            "row_content": "<p>No, grounding products do not emit EMF radiation, magnetic, or electric fields. They don’t use live electricity but simply connect you directly to the Earth’s natural energy. You can rest assured—grounding products are free of Wi-Fi, EMF signals, and electromagnetic fields.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_9XtYY9": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Why Can’t I Detect Continuity in My Grounding Cord?",
            "icon": "check_mark",
            "row_content": "<p>If you’re not detecting continuity in your grounding cord, it’s likely an issue with your multimeter settings. Our grounding cords include a 100,000 Ohm resistor, a safety feature designed to prevent any unexpected current from flowing through the cord while still allowing your body’s excess voltage to discharge safely into the ground.<br/><br/>Most multimeters use a continuity test to quickly check if a circuit is open or closed, but these tests are usually set to detect lower resistance values. Because of the high resistance of our grounding cord, the multimeter may not register continuity even though the cord is working perfectly.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_KCRTbQ": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Will It Work If I Live in an Apartment?",
            "icon": "check_mark",
            "row_content": "<p>Yes, our grounding products work perfectly in high-rise apartments. No matter which floor you live on, your grounding socket remains connected to the earth, allowing you to enjoy the full benefits of grounding.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_4MXy7T": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What If My Home Doesn’t Have a Grounding Outlet?",
            "icon": "check_mark",
            "row_content": "<p>If your home doesn’t have a grounding outlet, you can use our grounding rod. Simply place the rod into the earth outside, run the 40-foot cord into your home, and connect it to your Grounded Spirit product to enjoy the benefits of grounding.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_LyKaVq": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Will Grounding Products Interfere with My Pacemaker or Metal Implants?",
            "icon": "check_mark",
            "row_content": "<p>There is no evidence that grounding interferes with pacemakers or metal implants. Using grounding products is akin to walking barefoot or lying on the ground outdoors. No one with pacemakers or implants has been advised against barefoot contact with the earth.<br/><br/>Grounding also has an anticoagulant effect, which improves circulation and reduces the risk of blood clots. If you’re on blood-thinning medications, we recommend consulting your doctor before using grounding products.<br/><br/>Many of our customers with pacemakers or metal implants use grounding products without issues, but if you’re uncertain, it’s always best to consult with your healthcare provider.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_fakCzn": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Which Plug Type Should I Select?",
            "icon": "check_mark",
            "row_content": "<ul><li><strong>Canada and United States: </strong>Select the USA Plug option. This grounding wire plugs directly into the grounding socket of your outlet without an adaptor.</li><li><strong>United Kingdom: </strong>Select the UK Plug option.</li><li><strong>Germany, France, and other EU countries:</strong> Select the EU Plug option.</li><li><strong>Australia and New Zealand: </strong>Select the AU/NZ Plug option.</li><li><strong>Singapore and Malaysia: </strong>Select the UK Plug option.</li><li><strong>Indonesia: </strong>Select the EU Plug option for Type F sockets. </li></ul>",
            "page": ""
          }
        }
      },
